From 0a24430ed4f99a3998d032e755cd97a57d4fae29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Gillispie <27305807+kevingillispie@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Oct 2025 16:09:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] security: fix Stored XSS in JSON-LD output via post titles

- Sanitize `$page_title` using `sanitize_text_field()` before JSON encoding.
- Use `wp_json_encode()` with `JSON_HEX_*` flags to safely escape output.
- Fix breadcrumb titles with `sanitize_text_field()` to prevent injection.
- Secure `$path` extraction using `esc_url_raw()` and `parse_url()`.
- Update all comments to comply with WordPress Coding Standards (WPCS).

Resolves CVE pending assignment. Reported by Wordfence (Ticket 421133).
