Subject: [PATCH] fix(internal-helpers): improve isRemotePath to handle
 backslash URLs (#14408)

* fix(internal-helpers): improve isRemotePath to handle backslash URLs

Handle backslash patterns that could be normalized to remote URLs by browsers and runtimes. This includes single/double backslashes at the start, URL-encoded backslashes, and protocols with backslashes.

* add changeset

* test: update core-image test for improved path detection

Paths containing backslashes are now correctly identified as potential remote paths and return 403 (Forbidden) instead of 500. Update test expectations to handle both cases appropriately.

* test: fix core-image test expectations after path detection improvements

Use the actual isRemotePath function to determine expected status codes rather than pattern matching, ensuring test expectations align with the security fix behavior.
